WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.082 --> 00:00:02.177
- [Narrator] What was once a thick wall

00:00:02.177 --> 00:00:05.170
built to protect one of
Hungary's grandest castles

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.188
has been transformed into a lookout

00:00:07.188 --> 00:00:10.332
with the most beautiful and
panoramic views of Budapest.

00:00:10.332 --> 00:00:12.915
(lively music)

00:00:16.584 --> 00:00:19.741
The Fisherman's Bastion
is a 500-foot-long lookout

00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:22.471
located on the bank of the Danube River,

00:00:22.471 --> 00:00:25.863
and is one of the most visited
sites in all of Budapest.

00:00:25.863 --> 00:00:28.060
The site is only around
a hundred years old,

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.904
and was built in celebration
of the 1,000th birthday

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:33.549
of the Hungarian state.

00:00:33.549 --> 00:00:36.418
The neo-Romanesque
medieval-style architecture

00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:39.683
reflects the era the
first Hungarian king ruled

00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:41.100
in the year 1,000.

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:43.896
The Bastion's most distinguishing features

00:00:43.896 --> 00:00:45.458
are the seven turrets representing

00:00:45.458 --> 00:00:47.788
the seven Hungarian tribes who founded

00:00:47.788 --> 00:00:51.887
the present-day country in the year 895.

00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:54.656
The name, Fisherman's Bastion,
honors the guild of fisherman

00:00:54.656 --> 00:00:56.856
who protected the castle
from being destroyed

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.899
during the Middle Ages from enemies.

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:02.663
The intention in its construction
was to create a landmark

00:01:02.663 --> 00:01:06.036
that would showcase
Budapest's gorgeous views.

00:01:06.036 --> 00:01:09.590
Their success is evident, as
Fisherman's Bastion's archways,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.770
windows, and wide communal stairways

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.937
provide a view unlike any
other in all of Budapest.

